To teach multiplication principles to an 11-year-old student, a combination of visual aids, interactive exercises, and formative feedback mechanisms would be effective. The following pedagogical approach can be taken:
1. Start with the concept of repeated addition to introduce the idea of multiplication. Use visual aids such as arrays or groups of objects to illustrate the concept.
2. Introduce the times tables and use interactive exercises to help the student memorize them. These exercises can include quizzes, games, and flashcards.
3. Teach the associative and distributive properties of multiplication through examples and interactive exercises.
4. Use problem-solving scenarios to demonstrate practical applications of multiplication in real-life situations.
5. Incorporate the individual learning style of the student by using a variety of teaching methods such as visual aids, hands-on activities, and auditory cues.
6. Provide formative feedback mechanisms such as quizzes and assessments to track the student's progress over time.
Here is an example PHP code that can be used to create interactive exercises and track student progress in learning multiplication:
```
<?php
session_start();
// Set up multiplication table
$mult_table = array();
for ($i = 1; $i <= 10; $i++) {
  for ($j = 1; $j <= 10; $j++) {
    $mult_table[$i][$j] = $i * $j;
  }
}
// Check if answer is correct
function check_answer($answer, $mult_table, $row, $col) {
  if ($answer == $mult_table[$row][$col]) {
    $_SESSION['score']++;
    return true;
  } else {
    return false;
  }
}
// Display question and form
function display_question($mult_table, $row, $col) {
  echo "<p>What is " . $row . " x " . $col . "?</p>";
  echo "<form method='post'>";
  echo "<input type='number' name='answer'>";
  echo "<input type='hidden' name='row' value='" . $row . "'>";
  echo "<input type='hidden' name='col' value='" . $col . "'>";
  echo "<input type='submit' value='Submit'>";
  echo "</form>";
}
// Check if form has been submitted
if (isset($_POST['answer'])) {
  $answer = $_POST['answer'];
  $row = $_POST['row'];
  $col = $_POST['col'];
  if (check_answer($answer, $mult_table, $row, $col)) {
    echo "<p>Correct!</p>";
  } else {
    echo "<p>Incorrect. The answer is " . $mult_table[$row][$col] . ".</p>";
  }
}
// Display new question
$row = rand(1, 10);
$col = rand(1, 10);
display_question($mult_table, $row, $col);
// Display score
if (isset($_SESSION['score'])) {
  echo "<p>Score: " . $_SESSION['score'] . "</p>";
} else {
  $_SESSION['score'] = 0;
}
?>
```
This code creates a multiplication table and generates random questions for the student to answer. It checks if the answer is correct and provides formative feedback. It also tracks the student's score using session variables. This code can be modified to include different types of exercises and feedback mechanisms based on the individual learning style of the student.

