To sort the list of strings in descending order without using any built-in sorting functions, we can use a simple sorting algorithm like bubble sort. Here's the Java code implementation:
```java
public class StringSortDescending {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String[] fruits = {"apple", "orange", "banana", "grapefruit", "kiwi"};
        // sort the array in descending order
        for (int i = 0; i < fruits.length - 1; i++) {
            for (int j = i + 1; j < fruits.length; j++) {
                if (fruits[i].compareTo(fruits[j]) < 0) {
                    String temp = fruits[i];
                    fruits[i] = fruits[j];
                    fruits[j] = temp;
                }
            }
        }
        // print the sorted array
        for (String fruit : fruits) {
            System.out.println(fruit);
        }
    }
}
```
