Here's an HTML page with an input field where I can enter a string and a button to trigger the function in JavaScript:
```
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
	<title>Count Unique Characters</title>
</head>
<body>
	<label for="input">Enter a string:</label>
	<input type="text" id="input"><br><br>
	<button onclick="countUnique()">Count Unique Characters</button>
	<script>
		function countUnique() {
			// Get input value
			var input = document.getElementById("input").value;
			// Remove whitespace and convert to lowercase
			var str = input.replace(/\s/g, "").toLowerCase();
			// Create empty object to store characters and count
			var charCount = {};
			// Loop through string and add characters to object
			for (var i = 0; i < str.length; i++) {
				var char = str.charAt(i);
				if (charCount[char]) {
					charCount[char]++;
				} else {
					charCount[char] = 1;
				}
			}
			// Count number of unique characters
			var count = 0;
			for (var char in charCount) {
				if (charCount[char] === 1) {
					count++;
				}
			}
			// Display result
			alert("The number of unique characters in the string is: " + count);
		}
	</script>
</body>
</html>
```
This function will remove whitespace and convert all characters to lowercase, then create an empty object to store each character and its count. It will loop through the string and add each character to the object, increasing the count if it already exists. Finally, it will loop through the object and count the number of characters with a count of 1, indicating they are unique. The result will be displayed in an alert.

